@inherits Ti4ComponentBase

@*
    The speaker token. The word is part of the artwork, so there is one image per language and no text
    label beside it: `speaker.png` reads SPEAKER, `speaker_de.png` reads SPRECHER.

    English is the FALLBACK, not one case among equals — a language that has no marker of its own (any
    future one) gets the English token rather than nothing. So the switch names only the languages that
    actually have art.

    Inherits Ti4ComponentBase on purpose: the image now depends on the language, and without the base's
    Loc.OnChange subscription this component would keep the old token after an EN/DE toggle. A parent
    re-render is not enough — Blazor skips a child whose parameters didn't change, and SizeCss doesn't.

    Sized by height (width auto keeps the wide ~1.69:1 aspect).
*@
<img src="@Source" class="speaker-icon" alt="@Loc["players.speaker"]" title='@Loc["players.speaker"]'
     style="@(SizeCss is null ? null : $"height:{SizeCss}")" />

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? SizeCss { get; set; }

    private string Source => Loc.Lang switch
    {
        Language.De => "speaker_de.png",
        _ => "speaker.png"
    };
}
